('How does the taught full scan combine character and suffix pointer suggestions?','Take their maximum',['Add them','Take their minimum','Alternate them at random'],'Each gives an exclusion bound; the larger safe exclusion satisfies both.'),
('What happens on a successful character comparison?','Decrement both j and k',['Increment both j and k','Reset k=m immediately','Jump by charJump'],'Matching progresses leftwards within the current alignment.'),
('For WOWWOW, what are charJump[W], charJump[O] and an absent-character default?','0,1,6',['1,0,6','6,6,6','3,2,0'],'The rightmost W is position6, rightmost O position5, with m=6.'),
('When does this one-based scan return j+1 as a match?','After k reaches zero',['At every equal character','Whenever charJump is zero','At the first hash collision'],'Only complete matching of the pattern establishes an occurrence.'),
('At j=6,k=6,text character N absent from WOWWOW, what is the next endpoint?','12',['7','13','18'],'max(charJump[N]=6,matchJump[6]=1)=6; j becomes12.'),
('At mismatch j=9,k=3,text L absent, with matchJump[3]=6, where does j go?','15',['12','21','9'],'Take max(6,6)=6, not their sum12.'),
('At j=16,k=1,text M absent, with matchJump[1]=8, where does j go?','24',['22','30','18'],'The suffix suggestion8 exceeds charJump6; add8 to16.'),
